image:https://bevyengine.org/assets/bevy_logo_docs.svg[Bevy Logo,link=https://bevyengine.org]

A collection of mini-games implemented in Rust using the Bevy Engine as a learning exercise.

== Current Games

=== Pong
A classic Pong clone featuring:

* Two-player local gameplay
* Physics-based ball mechanics
* Customizable paddle movement
* Score tracking through goal detection

=== Tic-Tac-Toe
A work in progress implementation featuring:

* Customizable board size
* Chain length configuration for winning
* Basic board rendering

== Development Setup

=== Prerequisites

==== Installing Rust
[source,shell]
----
# Install Rust
curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://sh.rustup.rs | sh
----

==== System Dependencies

===== Ubuntu/Debian
[source,shell]
----
sudo apt-get install -y \
    pkg-config \
    libudev-dev \
    libasound2-dev \
    libx11-dev \
    libxcb-render0-dev \
    libxcb-shape0-dev \
    libxcb-xfixes0-dev
----

===== Fedora
[source,shell]
----
sudo dnf install -y \
    pkg-config \
    gcc \
    alsa-lib-devel \
    systemd-devel \
    libX11-devel \
    libxcb-devel \
    mesa-libGL-devel \
    vulkan-loader-devel \
    wayland-devel
----

===== Arch Linux
[source,shell]
----
sudo pacman -S --needed \
    pkg-config \
    gcc \
    alsa-lib \
    libx11 \
    libxcb \
    mesa \
    vulkan-icd-loader \
    wayland
----

===== macOS
[source,shell]
----
# Using Homebrew
brew install pkg-config
----

===== Windows

* Install Visual Studio 2019 or later with:
** "Desktop development with C++" workload
** Latest Windows 10 or 11 SDK
** Latest MSVC v143 build tools
** C++ CMake tools

Or using winget:
[source,shell]
----
winget install -e --id Microsoft.VisualStudio.2022.BuildTools
----

=== Building

[source,shell]
----
# Clone the repository
git clone [repository-url]
cd games

# Build in debug mode
cargo build

# Build in release mode
cargo build --release
----

=== Running

[source,shell]
----
# Run Pong
cargo run

# Run with debug rendering (shows physics boundaries)
cargo run --features debug
----

== Controls

=== Pong

[cols="1,2"]
|===
|Player |Controls

|Left Player
|kbd:[W] - Move Up +
kbd:[S] - Move Down

|Right Player
|kbd:[↑] - Move Up +
kbd:[↓] - Move Down
|===

== Technical Details

=== Architecture

* Built using the Bevy Engine's Entity Component System (ECS)
* Physics powered by bevy_rapier2d
* Custom color scheme using Oklch color space
* Modular code organization with separate modules for:
** Color definitions
** Game abstractions
** Individual game implementations

=== Window Configuration

* Resolution: 1280x720
* Windowed mode
* Custom clear color for consistent theming

